  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nBreezy northwest winds continue with a Lake Wind Advisory for Fort\nPeck Lake remaining in effect through 9 PM.\n\nClear skies will continue into tonight before upper ridging begins\nto rebound across the region into the middle of the week. This\nwill lead to warmer and drier weather conditions during that time.\n\nThe ridge axis will slide east into the Plains late into the \nweek with an increase in thunderstorms and a return to hot\ntemperatures. Some of the storms may produce locally heavy\nrainfall, but they will be isolated to scattered.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was blended with NBM90 for short term winds as wind speeds\nwere arriving on the higher side of the guidance envelope.\nOtherwise given warm and dry weather controlled by large scale\nridging for the next several days, NBM captured the expected\nforecast well with little to no deviations.",
